  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "jBhEvva7lb+1Eedw6dTq2i7P4wo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:26:31.494Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The research text for this group is two clauses long: not a complement, slot occupied, same displacement logic as Mendix. No demo, no integration point, and no OutSystems-specific reasoning is recorded \u2014 the conclusion is inherited from the Mendix analysis rather than derived independently.\n\nThat thinness is worth preserving as-is rather than dressing up. Anything more specific about how a displacement would work against OutSystems, or where its licence economics are weakest, would be new research and is not present in the corpus.\n\nThe cohort is six leads: three in PT, one each in NL, ES and DE. Their source rows record substantial partner standing \u2014 Elite, Premier and Premier Global tiers, one acquisition of another OutSystems consultancy \u2014 and five of the six are marked \"9 \u00b7 do not pitch\", with the remaining one at \"2 \u00b7 decide thesis first\". The qualification outcome and the partner depth point the same way, which is the practical reason this group produced a positioning note instead of a demo.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (6)\n\n**2 \u00b7 decide thesis first**\n- Truewind (now Axians) (PT)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- IG&H (NL \u00b7 mid)\n- ITSector (PT \u00b7 600+)\n- NTT Data Spain (ex-everis) (ES)\n- Noesis (PT \u00b7 3,500+ / 8 countries)\n- Valantic (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> NOT a complement \u2014 slot occupied. Same displacement logic as Mendix.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:26:31.494824Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:26:31.494828Z"
    }
  },
